{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/failure.py","reason":"Change 2 (group-classification core): replace the blanket `FallbackExceptionGroup -> CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL` arm in `_map` with a new `_classify_fallback_group` that aggregates an EXHAUSTED chain by its MOST-RECOVERABLE leg — a retryable leg (WAIT_AND_RETRY/RETRY_NOW) on ANY candidate wins, so a fallback leg's non-retryable failure can no longer mask a retryable primary throttle as INDETERMINATE. All-non-retryable groups keep CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL. Classifier stays TOTAL. Inherited by every gate surface at the single `interpret_failure`/preflight seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py","reason":"Change 1 (chain-construction core): make `should_fall_back` leg-aware — a NON-PRIMARY (fallback) leg's failure is always retained so the chain EXHAUSTS into a FallbackExceptionGroup instead of pydantic-ai bare-reraising the terminal leg and discarding the primary's retained cause; the PRIMARY keeps the deliberately narrow guard (credential/size/quota still fail loud, never masked). New `_wrap_fallback_leg` tags each non-primary candidate's exceptions in `build_fallback_model`. Applies to every chain the runner builds (runner.py:467)."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_throttle_no_failover_1c0d.py","reason":"NEW held-out oracle: (1) end-to-end through the real `build_fallback_model` + real `should_fall_back` — a throttled ModelHTTPError(429) primary behind a keyless-auth-TypeError fallback surfaces as exit-11 retryable (WAIT_AND_RETRY), not INDETERMINATE; (2) direct classifier — a group of [retryable 429, non-retryable TypeError] classifies retryable, order-independent; (3) over-broadening guard — an all-non-retryable group stays CHANGE_PROVIDER_OR_MODEL."}]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"FILE_IMPACT","timestamp":1788053924222132802,"uuid":"5f5ee51c-3ba3-409d-9683-68859bbc5e04"}